        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: હોડી",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "હોડી — hoḍī — \"boat, rowing boat\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "અમે હોડીમાં નદી ઓળંગી. — ame hoḍīmā̃ nadī oḷangī — \"We crossed the river in a boat.\""
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A feminine noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "હોડી (hoḍī) is listed by CDIAL, glossed \"boat\", under the lexical Sanskrit hōḍa, \"raft, boat\", which it takes from Dravidian, as in Kannada ōḍa, \"boat\" (CDIAL 14174). DEDR also judges the Indo-Aryan words probably Dravidian (DEDR 1039)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for everyday life at A2."
